[7m Manual page tar(1) line 31 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       device (e.g. a tape drive, hence the name of the program, which stands for [1mt[0mape [1mar[0mchiver),[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 32 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       which can be located either on the local or on a remote machine.[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 33 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 34 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K   [1mOption[0m [1mstyles[0m[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 35 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       Options  to  GNU  [1mtar[0m  can  be given in three different styles.  In [1mtraditional[0m [1mstyle[0m, the[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 36 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       first argument is a cluster of option letters and all subsequent  arguments  supply  argu‐[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 37 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       ments to those options that require them.  The arguments are read in the same order as the[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 38 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       option letters.  Any command line words that remain after all options has  been  processed[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 39 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       are treated as non-optional arguments: file or archive member names.[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 40 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 41 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       For example, the [1mc[0m option requires creating the archive, the [1mv[0m option requests the verbose[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 42 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       operation, and the [1mf[0m option takes an argument that sets the name of the archive to operate[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 43 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       upon.  The following command, written in the traditional style, instructs tar to store all[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 44 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       files from the directory [1m/etc[0m into the archive file [1metc.tar[0m verbosely  listing  the  files[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 45 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       being archived:[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 46 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 47 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       tar cfv etc.tar /etc[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 48 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 49 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       In  [1mUNIX[0m  or  [1mshort-option[0m [1mstyle[0m, each option letter is prefixed with a single dash, as in[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 50 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       other command line utilities.  If an option takes argument, the argument follows  it,  ei‐[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 51 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       ther  as  a  separate command line word, or immediately following the option.  However, if[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 52 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       the option takes an [1moptional[0m argument, the argument must follow the option letter  without[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 53 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       any intervening whitespace, as in [1m-g/tmp/snar.db[0m.[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 54 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 55 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       Any  number of options not taking arguments can be clustered together after a single dash,[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 56 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       e.g. [1m-vkp[0m.  Options that take arguments (whether mandatory or optional), can appear at the[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 57 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       end of such a cluster, e.g. [1m-vkpf[0m [1ma.tar[0m.[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 58 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 59 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       The example command above written in the [1mshort-option[0m [1mstyle[0m could look like:[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 60 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 61 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       tar -cvf etc.tar /etc[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 62 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       or[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 63 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       tar -c -v -f etc.tar /etc[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 64 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 65 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       In [1mGNU[0m or [1mlong-option[0m [1mstyle[0m, each option begins with two dashes and has a meaningful name,[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 66 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       consisting of lower-case letters and dashes.  When used, the long option can  be  abbrevi‐[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 67 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       ated  to  its initial letters, provided that this does not create ambiguity.  Arguments to[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 68 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       long options are supplied either as a separate command line  word,  immediately  following[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 69 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       the option, or separated from the option by an equals sign with no intervening whitespace.[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 70 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       Optional arguments must always use the latter method.[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 71 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 72 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       Here are several ways of writing the example command in this style:[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 73 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K[m
[7m Manual page tar(1) line 74 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K       tar --create --file etc.tar --verbose /etc[m
